{"version":1,"slug":"compound-interest","topic":"What is compound interest?","level":"beginner","title":"What Is Compound Interest?","summary":"You will understand how earning interest on your interest makes money grow faster and faster over time.","scopeNote":null,"scenes":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","title":"What is compound interest?","segments":[{"id":"intro-0","narration":"Imagine you save a hundred dollars, and it earns money while you sleep. How does a small pile quietly turn into a mountain?","sig":"ypUePmOpfyZxmhyuKr_QqY3M7fRJ6A5b","actions":[{"id":"hero","kind":"icon","cue":"Imagine you save","text":"Compound Interest","items":null,"icon":"piggy-bank","at":{"col":0,"row":1,"w":4,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"intro-1","narration":"Here's our plan. First, Interest on Your Interest. Then, The Snowball Effect. And finally, Time Is Your Superpower.","sig":"CbHWFwOZeh8Jv-iBoE2LnV-MqdnZYomx","actions":[{"id":"agenda","kind":"list","cue":"Here's our plan","text":null,"items":["Interest on Your Interest","The Snowball Effect","Time Is Your Superpower"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":1,"w":7,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c1","kind":"chapter","title":"Interest on Your Interest","segments":[{"id":"c1-0","narration":"Imagine you put some money into a savings account, like a digital piggy bank, and the bank pays you interest.","sig":"LEFG-7CTnDHlti31U65LpSA7lkhg9SSW","actions":[{"id":"piggy","kind":"icon","cue":"digital piggy bank","text":"Your Money","items":null,"icon":"piggy-bank","at":{"col":5,"row":0,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-1","narration":"With simple interest, you only ever earn interest on the original amount you put in.","sig":"cS_cffFWhTFPXkZBkd2X8yeT5RlqjlTB","actions":[{"id":"simple","kind":"box","cue":"With simple interest","text":"Simple: Original Only","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":2,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","cue":"original amount","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"piggy","to":"simple","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-2","narration":"With compound interest, you earn interest on your original money, plus all the interest you have already earned.","sig":"Bo3cNXICIxfqTB3Ri5f67fsA9ymVox90","actions":[{"id":"compound","kind":"box","cue":"With compound interest","text":"Compound: Original + Interest","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":7,"row":2,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"a2","kind":"arrow","cue":"original money","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"piggy","to":"compound","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-3","narration":"In other words, compound interest means you are earning interest on your interest, which helps your money grow much faster.","sig":"-R-C4L7nlfjSX60xHMuHp1RwjT5moP5u","actions":[{"id":"def","kind":"note","cue":"earning interest on your interest","text":"Interest on your interest","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":4,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"purple","expr":null},{"id":"hl","kind":"highlight","cue":"grow much faster","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"compound","color":null,"expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c2","kind":"chapter","title":"The Snowball Effect","segments":[{"id":"c2-0","narration":"Now that you know interest can earn its own interest, let us watch it roll like a snowball. Suppose you start with one hundred dollars at ten percent interest.","sig":"2cxGFDI56eAylvslSC6_rmtZCqqJ6wBQ","actions":[{"id":"growth","kind":"flow","cue":"watch it roll","text":null,"items":["Start: $100","Year 1: $110","Year 2: $121","Year 3: $133.10"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":12,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-1","narration":"After year one, you have one hundred ten dollars. Many people think you only earn ten dollars every year, but that is wrong.","sig":"d6BXKKwZiPSyKvE53tqTM5Dws5plwXm-","actions":[{"id":"wrong","kind":"box","cue":"only earn ten dollars","text":"Only +$10 every year","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":3,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"x1","kind":"cross_out","cue":"that is wrong","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"wrong","color":"red","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-2","narration":"Instead, you earn ten percent of your new, bigger total each time.","sig":"DlImb7lUHwS3PFDxh9Fvlw4AJtihCJGf","actions":[{"id":"right","kind":"box","cue":"new, bigger total","text":"10% of the new total","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":7,"row":3,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"c1","kind":"check","cue":"bigger total each time","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"right","color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-3","narration":"So in year two you earn eleven dollars, and in year three you reach one hundred thirty three dollars and ten cents.","sig":"rDqNdTN3mGiueIpNeNc6F7dTlRIkIDc2","actions":[{"id":"tr1","kind":"trace","cue":"in year two","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"growth","color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"h1","kind":"highlight","cue":"thirty three dollars","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"growth[3]","color":"green","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c3","kind":"chapter","title":"Time Is Your Superpower","segments":[{"id":"c3-0","narration":"That snowball effect is why time is your biggest superpower with compound interest. Look at what happens when we graph your money over many years.","sig":"Hsfn21B-KNg7Tr_n4fDU5ebB-eYbfXdS","actions":[{"id":"growth","kind":"plot","cue":"graph your money","text":"Money over time","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":"2^x; 0..5"}]},{"id":"c3-1","narration":"At first, the line barely climbs, so it feels like nothing is happening. But give it time, and the curve shoots straight up!","sig":"NilM4_0qTNfCdxXrSPz2gYQRrcaPAoF5","actions":[{"id":"c1","kind":"callout","cue":"barely climbs","text":"Slow at first","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"growth","color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"c2","kind":"callout","cue":"shoots straight up","text":"Fast later!","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"growth","color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-2","narration":"That is why starting early matters so much for your future. Even a small amount of money can grow huge if you just give it enough time.","sig":"i_q8MTfSk07Q6MpRNHWOH8lM-i8uhFJa","actions":[{"id":"clk","kind":"icon","cue":"starting early","text":"Start early","items":null,"icon":"clock","at":{"col":8,"row":1,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"key","kind":"note","cue":"give it enough time","text":"Time does the heavy lifting!","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":3,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"purple","expr":null},{"id":"h1","kind":"highlight","cue":"give it enough time","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"key","color":"green","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","title":"Recap","segments":[{"id":"recap-0","narration":"So remember: compound interest earns interest on your interest, grows like a rolling snowball, and works best when you start early. Do you have any questions for me?","sig":"02F6vWHbOO6idChe-xmGbWvSvZET-2sU","actions":[{"id":"recap_list","kind":"list","cue":"earns interest on your","text":null,"items":["Interest on your interest","Grows like a snowball","Starting early is key"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"recap_icon","kind":"icon","cue":"grows like a rolling","text":"Grow!","items":null,"icon":"trending-up","at":{"col":8,"row":2,"w":3,"h":3},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]}],"quiz":[{"question":"What makes compound interest different from simple interest?","options":["It only pays interest once","You earn interest on past interest","The bank charges a higher fee","It stays the exact same amount"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Compound interest adds your earned interest to your total, so you earn interest on your interest.","chapter":1},{"question":"You start with one hundred dollars at ten percent compound interest. How much do you earn in year two?","options":["Ten dollars","Nine dollars","Eleven dollars","Twelve dollars"],"answer":2,"explanation":"In year two, you earn ten percent of one hundred ten dollars, which is eleven dollars.","chapter":2},{"question":"Why is starting early so helpful with compound interest?","options":["The curve shoots up over time","Banks give teens higher rates","You never have to add money","It avoids paying any taxes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Compound interest grows slowly at first, then curves sharply upward if you give it enough time.","chapter":3}],"suggestions":["How does inflation affect your savings?","What is a stock market index?","How do credit card debts grow?"],"models":{"lesson":"google/gemini-4-hydrogen","voice":"openai/gpt-audio-mini (marin)"},"createdAt":"2026-11-17T08:00:45.723Z","audioBase":"/samples/compound-interest"}